<title>GERMANY: Eurofighter prototype has successful test - DASA.</title>
<headline>Eurofighter prototype has successful test - DASA.</headline>
<dateline>MANCHING, Germany 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German prototype of the Eurofighter combat jet project has just completed a successful week of test flights in Britain, Daimler-Benz Aerospace AG (DASA) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>DASA, a unit of car maker Daimler-Benz AG, said in a statement that test pilot Wolfgang Schirdewahn had made a series of low-level flights over the Irish Sea to test the aircraft's structural strength at supersonic speeds.</p>
<p>Using Tornado RB 199 jet engines, the DA1 model reached the highest top speed for a Eurofighter to date of 1.87 Mach. The Tornado engines have 20 percent less thrust than the EJ2000 power units with which other prototypes have been fitted.</p>
<p>DASA conducted the tests together with partner British Aerospace plc and said further joint tests were planned. The other members of the Eurofighter consortium are Alenia Spa of Italy and state-owned CASA of Spain.</p>
<p>Germany's government has put together 23 billion marks in financing to pay for the 180 Eurofighters it wants to buy to modernise its air force. Parliament is expected to vote on the procurement this autumn.</p>
</text>
